{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.StandardModel.ColourHeckeRegularHost","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.StandardModel.ColourHeckeRegularHost","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.FiniteDimensional.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Matrix.ToLin","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Matrix.Notation","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Dimension.Constructions","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Dimension.Finrank","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Algebra.Bilinear","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FinCases"],"declarations":22,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.ColourHeckeRegularHost.no_heckeCompatible_colour_action_on_regularH3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.ColourHeckeRegularHost.no_heckeCompatible_colour_action_on_regularH3","kind":"theorem","line":244,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/ColourHeckeRegularHost.lean#L244-L272","doc":"**G3 colour-action obstruction (scope-(b) structural exclusion).** No\nfaithful colour action of an 8-dimensional colour algebra `g` on the framework's\nown 6-dimensional regular three-strand Hecke state space can be **Hecke-\ncompatible** (commute with both braid generators `L₁, L₂`): such a `Φ` would\nland in the Hecke centralizer, whose dimension is `≤ 6 < 8`.\n\nThe invariant cited is the proved `finrank_heckeCentralizer_le_six`. Applies to\n`𝔰𝔲(3) = ker(ev_e)` via the corpus gate `finrank (su3 e) = 8`. It does **not**\nexclude the colour action on the Schur–Weyl tensor host `(ℂ³)^{⊗3}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.ColourHeckeRegularHost.finrank_heckeCentralizer_le_six","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.ColourHeckeRegularHost.finrank_heckeCentralizer_le_six","kind":"theorem","line":237,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/ColourHeckeRegularHost.lean#L237-L242","doc":"**The Hecke centralizer on the regular carrier is at most 6-dimensional.**\n`finrank(End_{H₃}(H₃)) ≤ finrank H₃ = 6`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.ColourHeckeRegularHost.finrank_V","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.ColourHeckeRegularHost.finrank_V","kind":"theorem","line":233,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/ColourHeckeRegularHost.lean#L233-L235","doc":"`finrank V = 6` (the regular carrier is 6-dimensional). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.ColourHeckeRegularHost.evAtOne_injective","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.ColourHeckeRegularHost.evAtOne_injective","kind":"theorem","line":215,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/ColourHeckeRegularHost.lean#L215-L229","doc":"**Evaluation at the cyclic vector is injective on the Hecke centralizer.**\nTwo centralizing endomorphisms agreeing at `e₀` agree everywhere. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.ColourHeckeRegularHost.centralizing_eval_zero_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.ColourHeckeRegularHost.centralizing_eval_zero_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":168,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/ColourHeckeRegularHost.lean#L168-L213","doc":"**A centralizing endomorphism is determined by its value on the cyclic\nvector.** If `T` commutes with `L₁, L₂` and kills `e₀`, then `T = 0`: it kills\neach basis word `eₖ = (L-word) e₀`, and those span `V`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.ColourHeckeRegularHost.evAtOne_apply","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.ColourHeckeRegularHost.evAtOne_apply","kind":"theorem","line":165,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/ColourHeckeRegularHost.lean#L165-L166","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.ColourHeckeRegularHost.evAtOne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.ColourHeckeRegularHost.evAtOne","kind":"def","line":161,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/ColourHeckeRegularHost.lean#L161-L163","doc":"Evaluation-at-`e₀` on the Hecke centralizer, `T ↦ T e₀`, as a linear map. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.ColourHeckeRegularHost.L1_sb4","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.ColourHeckeRegularHost.L1_sb4","kind":"theorem","line":154,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/ColourHeckeRegularHost.lean#L154-L157","doc":"`σ₁ · σ₂σ₁ = σ₁σ₂σ₁`: `L₁ e₄ = e₅`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.ColourHeckeRegularHost.L2_sb1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.ColourHeckeRegularHost.L2_sb1","kind":"theorem","line":149,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/ColourHeckeRegularHost.lean#L149-L152","doc":"`σ₂ · σ₁ = σ₂σ₁`: `L₂ e₁ = e₄`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.ColourHeckeRegularHost.L1_sb2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.ColourHeckeRegularHost.L1_sb2","kind":"theorem","line":144,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/ColourHeckeRegularHost.lean#L144-L147","doc":"`σ₁ · σ₂ = σ₁σ₂`: `L₁ e₂ = e₃`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.ColourHeckeRegularHost.L2_sb0","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.ColourHeckeRegularHost.L2_sb0","kind":"theorem","line":139,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/ColourHeckeRegularHost.lean#L139-L142","doc":"`σ₂ · 1 = σ₂`: `L₂ e₀ = e₂`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.ColourHeckeRegularHost.L1_sb0","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.ColourHeckeRegularHost.L1_sb0","kind":"theorem","line":134,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/ColourHeckeRegularHost.lean#L134-L137","doc":"`σ₁ · 1 = σ₁`: `L₁ e₀ = e₁`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.ColourHeckeRegularHost.sb_eq_basisFun","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.ColourHeckeRegularHost.sb_eq_basisFun","kind":"theorem","line":131,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/ColourHeckeRegularHost.lean#L131-L132","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.ColourHeckeRegularHost.sb","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.ColourHeckeRegularHost.sb","kind":"def","line":128,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/ColourHeckeRegularHost.lean#L128-L129","doc":"Standard basis vector `eᵢ` of the state space (`= Pi.basisFun ℚ (Fin 6) i`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.ColourHeckeRegularHost.mem_heckeCentralizer_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.ColourHeckeRegularHost.mem_heckeCentralizer_iff","kind":"theorem","line":114,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/ColourHeckeRegularHost.lean#L114-L119","doc":"Membership unfolds to the two commuting relations `T * Lᵢ = Lᵢ * T`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.ColourHeckeRegularHost.heckeCentralizer","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.ColourHeckeRegularHost.heckeCentralizer","kind":"def","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/ColourHeckeRegularHost.lean#L106-L112","doc":"The **Hecke centralizer**: endomorphisms of the state space commuting with\nboth regular Hecke generators — the target of a Hecke-compatible colour action\n(Schur–Weyl reading). A submodule as the intersection of the two commuting\nkernels. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.ColourHeckeRegularHost.L2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.ColourHeckeRegularHost.L2","kind":"def","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/ColourHeckeRegularHost.lean#L103-L104","doc":"Left-multiplication by `σ₂` as an endomorphism of the state space. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.ColourHeckeRegularHost.L1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.ColourHeckeRegularHost.L1","kind":"def","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/ColourHeckeRegularHost.lean#L100-L101","doc":"Left-multiplication by `σ₁` as an endomorphism of the state space. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.ColourHeckeRegularHost.M2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.ColourHeckeRegularHost.M2","kind":"def","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/ColourHeckeRegularHost.lean#L89-L98","doc":"Matrix of **left-multiplication by `σ₂`** on the regular carrier, copied\nfrom `QOU.Mathlib.HeckeAlgebra.H3.mulSigma2`. Output\n`(x₂, x₄, x₀+d·x₂, x₅, x₁+d·x₄, x₃+d·x₅)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.ColourHeckeRegularHost.M1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.ColourHeckeRegularHost.M1","kind":"def","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/ColourHeckeRegularHost.lean#L77-L87","doc":"Matrix of **left-multiplication by `σ₁`** on the regular carrier, copied\nfrom `QOU.Mathlib.HeckeAlgebra.H3.mulSigma1`. Row `i` = coefficients of the\n`i`-th output coordinate:\n`(x₁, x₀+d·x₁, x₃, x₂+d·x₃, x₅, x₄+d·x₅)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.ColourHeckeRegularHost.d","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.ColourHeckeRegularHost.d","kind":"def","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/ColourHeckeRegularHost.lean#L73-L75","doc":"Hecke off-diagonal weight `d = q − q⁻¹` (the coefficient in\n`σ_i² = (q − q⁻¹)σ_i + 1`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.ColourHeckeRegularHost.V","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.ColourHeckeRegularHost.V","kind":"def","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/ColourHeckeRegularHost.lean#L68-L71","doc":"The framework's 6-dimensional regular three-strand Hecke state space,\n`H3Carrier = ℚ⁶` (basis `{1, σ₁, σ₂, σ₁σ₂, σ₂σ₁, σ₁σ₂σ₁}` at positions `0..5`),\nmodelled as `Fin 6 → ℚ`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}